layout "layout.faqir"

block content
  p
    | A repository describes its
    strong line
    | in one small file,
    code factory.json
    | , at the top of its main checkout. The line says how to set the repository up, which commands check a package, where the acceptance tests and screenshots go, and which files a worker may not touch. Everything else (worktrees, QA, the review, the visual check, integration and cleanup) is built into the factory: the
    strong kit
    | , which the
    a(href="/docs/runner") runner
    | carries.
  h2#file The file
  ul
    li
      | Everything is optional.
      code { "commands": { "verify": "npm test" } }
      | is a working line: G1 runs the tests, G3 reviews the change, G5 integrates it.
    li
      | The runner reads the file in the project's
      strong main checkout
      | , never in a worker's worktree, so a worker cannot change its own gates. A package that changes the line file does so only through G5 and only with your approval.
    li
      | Command lines run through the shell (the platform's by default:
      code cmd.exe
      | on Windows,
      code /bin/sh
      | elsewhere), in the package's worktree, with
      a(href="#placeholders") placeholders
      | filled from checked values only.
      code commands.cleanup
      | runs in the main checkout.
    li
      | Keys starting with
      code $
      | or
      code //
      | are comments. The runner reports the resolved line to Buildyboy on every
      code prepare
      | and when you press
      strong Check setup
      | ; the project's Setup tab shows it, or the error.
    li
      | A project's overrides (Setup tab, or an operator's
      code projects_save
      | ) win over the file for
      code limits.workers
      | ,
      code limits.rounds
      | ,
      code models.*
      | and
      code integrate.approval
      | .
  h2#keys Every key
  div(data-ui="table")
    table(data-part="table")
      thead(data-part="thead")
        tr(data-part="tr")
          th(data-part="th" scope="col") Key
          th(data-part="th" scope="col") What it does, and its default
      tbody(data-part="tbody")
        tr(data-part="tr")
          td(data-part="td")
            code base
          td(data-part="td")
            | The branch packages are integrated into. Default:
            code main
            | .
        tr(data-part="tr")
          td(data-part="td")
            code branch
          td(data-part="td")
            | The package's branch. Must contain an id placeholder. Default:
            code pkg/{id}
            | .
        tr(data-part="tr")
          td(data-part="td")
            code worktree
          td(data-part="td")
            | The package's worktree, relative to the checkout or absolute. It must be inside the runner's allowed folders. Default:
            code ../<checkout folder>-wt/{id}
            | .
        tr(data-part="tr")
          td(data-part="td")
            code shell
          td(data-part="td")
            | The argv that runs a command line, for example
            code ["C:/Program Files/Git/bin/bash.exe", "-c"]
            | for POSIX commands on Windows. Default: the platform's shell.
        tr(data-part="tr")
          td(data-part="td")
            code commands.setup
          td(data-part="td")
            | Runs once the worktree exists: install dependencies, create a database. Default: none.
        tr(data-part="tr")
          td(data-part="td")
            code commands.verify
          td(data-part="td")
            | G1: typecheck, lint, tests. Without it G1 is off. Default: none.
        tr(data-part="tr")
          td(data-part="td")
            code commands.acceptance
          td(data-part="td")
            | G2: the package's acceptance tests. Without it G2 and QA are off. Default: none.
        tr(data-part="tr")
          td(data-part="td")
            code commands.shots
          td(data-part="td")
            | G4: writes screenshots of the package's pages to
            code paths.shots
            | . Without it G4 is off. Default: none.
        tr(data-part="tr")
          td(data-part="td")
            code commands.app
          td(data-part="td")
            | G4: starts the app for the visual judge, at
            code app.url
            | (default
            code http://localhost:{port}
            | ); it waits for
            code app.readyPath
            | (
            code /
            | ) for up to
            code app.readyTimeoutSec
            | (180) seconds. Default: none.
        tr(data-part="tr")
          td(data-part="td")
            code commands.cleanup
          td(data-part="td")
            | After integration, in the main checkout: drop the package's database. Default: none.
        tr(data-part="tr")
          td(data-part="td")
            code paths.packages
          td(data-part="td")
            | The package specs: Markdown with frontmatter (
            a(href="/docs/planning#spec") Planning
            | ). Default:
            code factory/packages
            | .
        tr(data-part="tr")
          td(data-part="td")
            code paths.acceptance
          td(data-part="td")
            | Where QA writes the package's acceptance tests. A worker may not change them. Default:
            code tests/acceptance/{localId}
            | .
        tr(data-part="tr")
          td(data-part="td")
            code paths.shots
          td(data-part="td")
            | Screenshots for G4; at most 12 are attached to the gate. Default:
            code test-results/shots/{localId}
            | .
        tr(data-part="tr")
          td(data-part="td")
            code paths.protected
          td(data-part="td")
            | More paths a worker may not change (
            a(href="#protected") below
            | ). Default:
            code []
            | .
        tr(data-part="tr")
          td(data-part="td")
            code env
            | ,
            code envFile
          td(data-part="td")
            | Variables for every step and the worker, also written to this file in the worktree and kept out of git. Default:
            code {}
            | ,
            code .env.factory
            | .
        tr(data-part="tr")
          td(data-part="td")
            code resources
          td(data-part="td")
            code ports: [from, to]
            | ,
            code dbPrefix
            | ,
            code migrations: {from, block}
            | : what a claim hands each package. Without it, a project migrated from the old per-repo settings keeps those. Default: none.
        tr(data-part="tr")
          td(data-part="td")
            code gates.G1
            | …
            code gates.G5
          td(data-part="td")
            code enabled
            | ,
            code timeoutSec
            | ,
            code steps
            | (argv steps that replace the built-in gate);
            code G2.qa
            | (true),
            code G3.security
            | (
            code sensitive
            | ,
            code always
            | or
            code never
            | ),
            code G4.chrome
            | (false),
            code G5.push
            | (true). Default: on when their command exists; G3 and G5 always.
        tr(data-part="tr")
          td(data-part="td")
            code steps.prepare
            | ,
            code .qa
            | ,
            code .cleanup
            | ,
            code .revert
          td(data-part="td")
            code steps
            | (argv steps that replace the built-in step),
            code timeoutSec
            | . Default: built in.
        tr(data-part="tr")
          td(data-part="td")
            code models
          td(data-part="td")
            | The model per role.
            code foreman: null
            | turns the foreman off: every question goes to you. Default:
            code opus
            | for worker, qa, review, foreman and planner;
            code sonnet
            | for visual.
        tr(data-part="tr")
          td(data-part="td")
            code worker
          td(data-part="td")
            | How a worker starts: in a herdr terminal (
            code hc
            | ) or as a headless
            code claude -p
            | job (
            code claude
            | ). Default:
            code launcher: hc
            | ,
            code permissionMode: auto
            | ,
            code limitHours: 10
            | ,
            code subagents: 4
            | ,
            code chrome: false
            | .
        tr(data-part="tr")
          td(data-part="td")
            code limits
          td(data-part="td")
            | How many packages of this project are in flight at once;
            code rounds
            | overrides the gate round limit. Default:
            code workers: 2
            | .
        tr(data-part="tr")
          td(data-part="td")
            code integrate.approval
          td(data-part="td")
            | When to ask you before G5:
            code never
            | ,
            code sensitive
            | (packages flagged sensitive) or
            code always
            | . Default:
            code sensitive
            | .
        tr(data-part="tr")
          td(data-part="td")
            code context
          td(data-part="td")
            | Files every role reads first. Default:
            code ["CLAUDE.md"]
            | .
        tr(data-part="tr")
          td(data-part="td")
            code timeoutSec
          td(data-part="td")
            | The default timeout of every argv step (a §11.7 recipe's key). Default: none.
  h2#gates Which gates run
  dl
    dt
      | G1 · build and tests
    dd
      | Runs
      code commands.verify
      | . The summary keeps the last result lines and the first error lines.
    dt
      | G2 · acceptance
    dd
      | Fails if the package's acceptance folder differs from what QA committed, or if the branch touched other packages' acceptance tests; then runs
      code commands.acceptance
      | . A
      code MANUAL.md
      | there is named in the summary: checks for you to do by hand.
    dt
      | QA, before the build
    dd
      | When G2 is on and
      code G2.qa
      | is true, a
      code claude -p
      | session writes one black-box test per acceptance criterion in
      code paths.acceptance
      | , before any code exists, commits them and tags the commit. It follows
      code factory/qa.md
      | if the repository has one.
    dt
      | G3 · review
    dd
      | Always on. A read-only
      code claude -p
      | reviewer judges the diff against the package's spec, the context files and
      code factory/review.md
      | ; a second pass looks only at security when
      code G3.security
      | asks for it (by default for packages flagged sensitive). Any blocker or major fails it. From round 2 it checks the earlier findings first.
    dt
      | G4 · visual
    dd
      | Runs
      code commands.shots
      | , starts
      code commands.app
      | , and a
      code claude -p
      | judge reads the screenshots (and the live app in Chrome when
      code G4.chrome
      | is true) against
      code factory/visual.md
      | . Skipped when the package produced no screenshots.
    dt
      | G5 · integration
    dd
      | Always on. Merges
      code origin/<base>
      | into the branch (a conflict fails with the files), runs G1 and G2 again on the result, then fast-forwards
      code <base>
      | in the main checkout and pushes. It stops for your approval when protected paths changed, or when
      code integrate.approval
      | says so.
  p
    | Set
    code "enabled": false
    | on a gate to turn it off;
    code "enabled": true
    | without its command is an error. A gate's argv
    code steps
    | replace the built-in, with the contract of the old recipes (
    a(href="#legacy") below
    | ).
  h2#protected What a worker may not change
  p
    code factory.json
    | itself and every package's acceptance folder are always protected.
    code paths.protected
    | adds more: a folder (
    code .github/workflows/
    | ), a file (
    code deploy/prod.env.example
    | ) or a pattern (
    code db/migrations/0*.sql
    | , where
    code *
    | matches within one folder and
    code **
    | across folders). Three things enforce it:
  ul
    li
      | the worker's brief tells it so;
    li
      | the plugin's
      a(href="/docs/skills#guard") guard
      | refuses a worker's edits to those paths while it works;
    li
      | G2 fails when acceptance tests changed, and G5 stops with
      strong needs approval
      | when the branch changed a protected path: it integrates only once you agree.
  h2#placeholders Placeholders
  p
    | Commands, paths,
    code env
    | values, the branch and the worktree may use these. Values that are not plain are quoted for the line's shell.
  div(data-ui="table")
    table(data-part="table")
      thead(data-part="thead")
        tr(data-part="tr")
          th(data-part="th" scope="col") Placeholder
          th(data-part="th" scope="col") Value for package SH-P1 of project shop-api
      tbody(data-part="tbody")
        tr(data-part="tr")
          td(data-part="td")
            code {id}
            | ,
            code {idLower}
          td(data-part="td")
            code SH-P1
            | ,
            code sh-p1
        tr(data-part="tr")
          td(data-part="td")
            code {localId}
            | ,
            code {localIdLower}
          td(data-part="td")
            code P1
            | ,
            code p1
            | : the id without the project's prefix
        tr(data-part="tr")
          td(data-part="td")
            code {project}
          td(data-part="td")
            code shop-api
        tr(data-part="tr")
          td(data-part="td")
            code {round}
          td(data-part="td")
            | the current gate round,
            code 1
            | ,
            code 2
            | …
        tr(data-part="tr")
          td(data-part="td")
            code {port}
            | ,
            code {db}
          td(data-part="td")
            | the port and database name the claim allocated (empty without
            code resources
            | )
        tr(data-part="tr")
          td(data-part="td")
            code {worktree}
            | ,
            code {branch}
          td(data-part="td")
            | the worktree's absolute path and the branch
  h2#examples Three examples
  h3#library A library with only tests
  pre
    code
      | {
      |   "commands": {
      |     "setup": "npm ci",
      |     "verify": "npm run typecheck && npm test"
      |   }
      | }
  p
    | G1 runs the tests, G3 reviews every change, G5 merges into
    code main
    | and pushes. There are no acceptance tests (G2 and QA are off) and no screenshots (G4 is off). Adding
    code commands.acceptance
    | later switches on QA and G2, the factory's strongest check: tests written from the criteria before the code, that the worker cannot change.
  h3#web-app A web app with acceptance tests and screenshots
  pre
    code
      | {
      |   "commands": {
      |     "setup": "pnpm install --frozen-lockfile && pnpm db:create {db}",
      |     "verify": "pnpm typecheck && pnpm lint && pnpm test",
      |     "acceptance": "pnpm exec playwright test tests/acceptance/{localId}",
      |     "shots": "pnpm shots {localId}",
      |     "app": "pnpm dev --port {port}",
      |     "cleanup": "pnpm db:drop {db}"
      |   },
      |   "app": { "url": "http://localhost:{port}", "readyPath": "/health" },
      |   "env": { "PORT": "{port}", "DATABASE_URL": "postgres://localhost:5432/{db}" },
      |   "resources": { "ports": [4100, 4199], "dbPrefix": "shop_", "migrations": { "from": 100, "block": 10 } },
      |   "paths": { "protected": [".github/workflows/", "db/migrations/0*.sql"] },
      |   "gates": { "G4": { "chrome": true } },
      |   "integrate": { "approval": "always" },
      |   "limits": { "workers": 3 },
      |   "context": ["CLAUDE.md", "docs/architecture.md"]
      | }
  p
    | Every gate runs. Each package gets its own port from 4100–4199, its own database
    code shop_<id>
    | and ten migration numbers, so three packages build side by side without stepping on each other.
    code pnpm shots P1
    | must write the package's pages to
    code test-results/shots/P1
    | (the default
    code paths.shots
    | ). The visual judge also opens the running app in Chrome. Nothing is integrated without your yes.
  h3#legacy A legacy recipe
  pre
    code
      | {
      |   "timeoutSec": 1800,
      |   "gates": {
      |     "G1": { "steps": [{ "name": "verify", "argv": ["bash", "{recipeDir}/scripts/g1.sh", "{id}", "{round}"] }] },
      |     "G2": { "steps": [{ "name": "acceptance", "argv": ["bash", "{recipeDir}/scripts/g2.sh", "{id}", "{port}"] }] },
      |     "G3": { "steps": [{ "name": "review", "argv": ["bash", "{recipeDir}/scripts/g3.sh", "{id}", "{args}"] }] }
      |   }
      | }
  p
    | A file with argv
    code steps
    | and no
    code commands
    | is a recipe of the earlier factory: a project migrated from the old per-repo settings points at one (for example
    code fabrica/porti/porti.json
    | ). It runs exactly as before: only its argv steps, in the main checkout, without a shell; a gate without steps answers "recipe has no G4"; the kit's
    code prepare
    | ,
    code qa
    | and
    code cleanup
    | are off, so a coordinator prepares worktrees itself: keep the autopilot off for such a project. Each step exits 0 for pass (or skip), 1 for fail, anything else for an error, and prints a last line of JSON:
    code {"verdict", "summary", "details", "findings", "shots"}
    | . The placeholders
    code {recipeDir}
    | and
    code {args}
    | exist only here. Add
    code commands
    | to move such a repository onto the kit; argv
    code steps
    | can stay to override single gates.
  h2#check Checking a line
  ul
    li
      | On any machine with a Buildyboy checkout:
      code node cli/bb.ts line check <repo>
      | (
      code --file
      | for another line file,
      code --id
      | for a sample package id,
      code --json
      | for the whole resolved line). It reads only and runs nothing: it prints the gates that run, every command filled in for a sample package, the worktree and the paths, or every error with exit code 1.
    li
      code node cli/bb.ts doctor
      | , run in the repository, says whether its
      code factory.json
      | is valid.
    li
      | On the project's
      strong Setup
      | tab,
      strong Check setup
      | asks the project's runner to read and validate the line where it really runs; the result, or the error, stays on the page.
